// @@@ The last index of a value in the list remains the same if the value is not in the list. For any index i that is greater than the last index and less than the size of the list, the element at index i is null if the value o is null, or the element at index i is not equal to the value o.

--------------------
// @@@ The return value of the lastIndexOf method is either the index of the last occurrence of the specified element in the vector, or -1 if the vector does not contain the element. If the vector contains the element, then for all indices i that are greater than the return value and less than the size of the vector, the element at index i is either null (if the specified element is null) or not equal to the specified element.

